{"id":"40368e43da5f58fb","group":"93","path":"93/93-df-congruence-extension.md","title":"Congruence Extension","display":"df-congruence-extension — Congruence Extension","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-df-congruence-extension","aliases":["93-df-congruence-extension"],"display":"df-congruence-extension — Congruence Extension","depends_on":["[[93-df-congruence]]","[[93-df-subalgebra]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-df-congruence-extension"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-df-congruence-extension</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-congruence-extension — Congruence Extension"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"30b341bfbd8b5301\" href=\"?note=30b341bfbd8b5301\" title=\"93-df-congruence\">93-df-congruence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"154cc3ca1a9b40e2\" href=\"?note=154cc3ca1a9b40e2\" title=\"93-df-subalgebra\">93-df-subalgebra</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf A\">\\(\\mathbf A\\)</span> is an algebra candidate and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\mathbf B|\">\\(|\\mathbf B|\\)</span> denotes the carrier of a subalgebra.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}\">\\(\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}\\)</span> is the algebra predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"6730349967b8ffce\" href=\"?note=6730349967b8ffce\" title=\"93-df-algebra\">93-df-algebra</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Subalg}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Subalg}_{93}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Con}\">\\(\\mathrm{Con}\\)</span> are the predicates of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"154cc3ca1a9b40e2\" href=\"?note=154cc3ca1a9b40e2\" title=\"93-df-subalgebra\">93-df-subalgebra</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"30b341bfbd8b5301\" href=\"?note=30b341bfbd8b5301\" title=\"93-df-congruence\">93-df-congruence</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CEP}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{CEP}_{93}\\)</span> is defined here.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}congruence\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\\mathrm{CEP}_{93}(\\mathbf A)\\leftrightarrow\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\Bigl[{}&amp;\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle}(\\mathbf A)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\mathbf B\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Subalg}_{93}(\\mathbf B,\\mathbf A)\\to\\forall\\theta\\;\\bigl(\\theta\\in\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf B)\\to\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{7em}\\exists\\phi\\;(\\phi\\in\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf A)\\land\\theta=\\phi\\cap(|\\mathbf B|\\times|\\mathbf B|))\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}congruence\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\\mathrm{CEP}_{93}(\\mathbf A)\\leftrightarrow\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\Bigl[{}&amp;\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle}(\\mathbf A)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\mathbf B\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Subalg}_{93}(\\mathbf B,\\mathbf A)\\to\\forall\\theta\\;\\bigl(\\theta\\in\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf B)\\to\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{7em}\\exists\\phi\\;(\\phi\\in\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf A)\\land\\theta=\\phi\\cap(|\\mathbf B|\\times|\\mathbf B|))\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Restriction is taken to the actual carrier square of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf B\">\\(\\mathbf B\\)</span>; the similarity type of the one-place predicate is recovered from <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf A\">\\(\\mathbf A\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-congruence","status":"resolved","id":"30b341bfbd8b5301","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-congruence]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-subalgebra","status":"resolved","id":"154cc3ca1a9b40e2","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-subalgebra]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-algebra","status":"resolved","id":"6730349967b8ffce","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}$ is the algebra predicate of [[93-df-algebra]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-subalgebra","status":"resolved","id":"154cc3ca1a9b40e2","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Subalg}_{93}$ and $\\mathrm{Con}$ are the predicates of [[93-df-subalgebra]] and [[93-df-congruence]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-congruence","status":"resolved","id":"30b341bfbd8b5301","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Subalg}_{93}$ and $\\mathrm{Con}$ are the predicates of [[93-df-subalgebra]] and [[93-df-congruence]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathbf A","display":false},{"tex":"|\\mathbf B|","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Subalg}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Con}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CEP}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}congruence\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\\mathrm{CEP}_{93}(\\mathbf A)\\leftrightarrow\\exists S\\;\\exists\\alpha\\;\\Bigl[{}&\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\langle S,\\alpha\\rangle}(\\mathbf A)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall\\mathbf B\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Subalg}_{93}(\\mathbf B,\\mathbf A)\\to\\forall\\theta\\;\\bigl(\\theta\\in\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf B)\\to\\\\\n&\\hspace{7em}\\exists\\phi\\;(\\phi\\in\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathbf A)\\land\\theta=\\phi\\cap(|\\mathbf B|\\times|\\mathbf B|))\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbf B","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbf A","display":false}],"bytes":1311,"backlinks":[{"id":"803e6b0ea3bd8453","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"e6fd74a4291b286e","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"Congruence extension is an additional property of $\\mathbf A$; it is false for arbitrary algebras.  The legacy label is retained, but the statement is an instance of [[93-df-congruence-extension]], not an unconditional Maltsev lemma."}],"outgoing":["30b341bfbd8b5301","154cc3ca1a9b40e2","6730349967b8ffce"]}